  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Present perfect = have / has + participio pasado**",
      "",
      "| | Forma | Ejemplo |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| Afirmativa | I / you / we / they **have** · he / she / it **has** + participio | *I've seen it. · She has been there.* |",
      "| Negativa | **haven't / hasn't** + participio | *I haven't eaten sushi.* |",
      "| Pregunta | **Have / Has** + sujeto + participio? | *Have you ever been to Spain?* |",
      "| Respuesta corta | Yes, I **have**. / No, I **haven't**. | *Yes, she has.* |",
      "",
      "**Participios:** regulares = *-ed* (*visited, tried, worked*). Irregulares (hay que aprenderlos): *be → **been** · go → **gone** · see → **seen** · eat → **eaten** · do → **done** · write → **written** · take → **taken** · have → **had** · make → **made** · meet → **met** · buy → **bought** · fly → **flown** · drive → **driven***.",
      "",
      "**Been vs gone:** *She has been to Paris* (fue y ya volvió) ≠ *She has gone to Paris* (está allí ahora).",
      "",
      "**Usamos el present perfect** para experiencias de la vida sin decir cuándo: *I've been to London.* Si dices cuándo (*last year*), usas pasado simple (lo vemos en la lección 4).",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *been* /biːn/ · *seen* /siːn/ · *eaten* /ˈiːtn/ · contracciones *I've* /aɪv/, *she's* /ʃiːz/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I have went to London.",
        "right": "I have been to London.",
        "note": "Went es pasado; el participio de go es gone y para visitas se usa been."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "Did you ever eat sushi?",
        "right": "Have you ever eaten sushi?",
        "note": "Para experiencias de vida se usa el present perfect."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
